menu "Slave OTA"

config P3A_SLAVE_OTA_MOCK
    bool "Mock slave OTA (test screen ownership without real OTA)"
    default n
    help
      When enabled, slave_ota_check_and_update runs through all the UX
      paths (UI ownership, input lockout, success countdown, reboot)
      but does NOT call esp_hosted_slave_ota_*. Used to verify the
      screen-owning code without burning real OTA cycles. Disable
      before shipping.

config P3A_SLAVE_OTA_MOCK_DURATION_MS
    int "Total mock duration (ms)"
    depends on P3A_SLAVE_OTA_MOCK
    default 10000
    range 2000 60000
    help
      How long the mock OTA takes to climb from 0% to 100%, in
      milliseconds. Defaults to 10 seconds, similar to a real ~1 MB
      transfer over SDIO. Bump this when manually testing the input
      lockout to give yourself a wider window to press buttons or
      issue commands.

endmenu

# Not options: three hidden constants, all 0.
#
# esp_hosted releases newer than the one pinned in this component's
# idf_component.yml make three USB host libraries conditional on these
# symbols (rules of the form "$CONFIG{...} == 1"). When the component manager
# resolves dependencies on a machine without a warm cache (a CI runner, a new
# workstation) it reads those newer manifests too, and the IDF then aborts the
# configure step with "Missing required kconfig option after retry", because
# no Kconfig file defines the symbols: the pinned esp_hosted predates them.
# Defining them here as 0 lets the resolver evaluate the rules (false: p3a
# reaches the co-processor over SDIO, not USB) and carry on.
#
# They are integers because the rules compare them with 1; the resolver
# rejects a boolean there.
#
# Remove them when esp_hosted is bumped to a release that defines the symbols
# itself; Kconfig will then report them as defined in two places.
config ESP_HOSTED_HOST_USB_CDC_ACM_MANIFEST
    int
    default 0

config ESP_HOSTED_HOST_USB_CHERRYUSB_MANIFEST
    int
    default 0

config ESP_HOSTED_HOST_USB_RNDIS_MANIFEST
    int
    default 0
